 "finding": "An oracle told the exact reflectivity, the background motion, the shaking's realisation and both physical models, lacking only which is true and the receiver noise, is bounded exactly: its detection rate exceeds its false-alarm rate by 2 Phi(Delta / 2) - 1, and no method told less does better, whatever the ground's texture. Pulse by pulse on the real dwell the formula for Delta holds (0.993 +- 0.025 of it; 1.011 +- 0.030 with the background ten times larger, which cancels). At 30 dB per resolution cell, under the ambient levels the bench room gives the oracle at most 1.2e-04: its imprint would have to grow 1.1e+04 times, 1.2e+02 after allowing the local level ten times the regional, site amplification three times and 10 dB more SNR. The open regime is strong nearby shaking known exactly: truck over a bump 15 m away, all pass, at 72 Hz (surface_favourable) gives the oracle 0.99, 0.6 times short of 95% found at 5% false alarms, which the allowances erase (14 cases open). Depth is another matter: rooms 15 m down, small and spread, match the mark of a room 30 m down to 71.3% (the bench room itself only to 78%), so telling the two depths apart takes 1 times the signal that detecting either takes, for any method; the superposition of small rooms holds to 3.7%."
}